## ★ SESSION 9 — INVARIANTS ENFORCED + FULL AUDIT (2026-07-27, PRs #29 / #30)
> Full findings: `docs/AUDIT_2026-07-27.md`. PR #28 and #29 merged to Develop.
- [x] **INVARIANT-2/3 now actually enforced** (PR #29). The plugin had never been loaded by any
      ESLint config. Scoped to `src/routes/**` (option (a) from phase2-proposal §3); workers and
      the pre-auth bootstrap use the privileged pool by design. 7 justified line-level disables;
      `reportUnusedDisableDirectives: 'error'` so a stale one fails the build. Two rule bugs fixed:
      `app.delete()` was read as a DB write, and `no-hostel-id-from-request` only matched `req`
      while every route names it `request` — its "0 violations" meant nothing. Rules now have
      RuleTester regression tests in CI.
- [x] **Real violation found + fixed**: `POST /auth/totp/setup` runs authenticated → now uses
      withTenant; its two UPDATEs collapsed into one statement in that transaction (a failure
      between them left an account with a TOTP secret and no backup codes). 2 new tests.
- [x] **CNIC gate CLOSED** — verified live: only `students.cnic_encrypted` exists, 0 non-AES-GCM
      values. `backfill-cnic.mjs` is a no-op (prod holds 1 student, 0 CNICs). No founder action.
- [x] **DLQ false-positive bug fixed** — workers called `moveToDLQ` on EVERY failed attempt, so a
      job that later succeeded still wrote rows to `dlq_jobs`. Guard added inside `moveToDLQ`
      (one definition of "exhausted" for all 5 workers) + test.
- [x] **3 dead deps removed** — `@fastify/jwt` (never imported; all JWT via `jose`),
      `@fastify/rate-limit`, `@otplib/preset-default`. Killed 3 CRITICAL CVEs incl. fast-jwt cache
      confusion. `pnpm audit` 42→36, criticals 5→2 (both non-runtime: vitest, bcrypt's tar).

### ⚠️ AUDIT FINDINGS NEEDING YOUR DECISION (details in docs/AUDIT_2026-07-27.md)
- [ ] **🔴 Prod has NO `schema_migrations` ledger** — hand-migrated, never baselined. Staging has
      all 11. Prod also still has legacy `users.totp_secret` (0 rows) that a from-scratch DB lacks,
      so **staging is not a faithful rehearsal of prod**. Fix = `migrate.mjs baseline` against prod
      then `DROP COLUMN totp_secret`. Both are prod writes → yours to authorise. Safe only while
      there is no real data.
- [ ] **🔴 Fastify 4.29.1 is EOL** — every remaining runtime CVE traces to it (body-validation
      bypass, X-Forwarded spoofing, HTTP/2 DDoS, fast-uri host confusion) and every patch is on
      5.x. Also blocks `@fastify/multipart` v8→v10. Schedule 4→5 as the first Phase-2 infra task.
- [ ] **🟠 Authorization matrix incoherent** — `chain_manager` can `reveal-cnic` and bulk-import
      students but cannot list or read one; every other module treats it as owner-equivalent. And
      the `viewer` role is in the DB CHECK but in **zero** `requireRole` calls — it 403s everywhere.
- [ ] 🟡 Isolation tests cover 3 of 16 route modules; PRD gate says every endpoint (~half a day).
- [ ] 🟡 11 merged remote branches to delete.

## ★ SESSION 8 — PHASE 1 CODE BACKLOG CLOSED (2026-07-26, PR #28, branch `test/phase1-gate`)
> Every item below is CI-verified on real Postgres+Redis. Suite: **7 files / 38 tests, 0 skipped.**
- [x] **Isolation gate GREEN** (run 30224319107) — isolation 10/10, auth 5/5, dlq 2/2. Verified
      from the job log that the tests RAN: with `DATABASE_URL` unset they skip and CI still
      reports success, so the green tick alone proves nothing.
- [x] **pg pools kept warm** (`191318b`) — `/ready` was ~425ms of TCP+TLS handshake to Supabase
      Mumbai on every probe, because pg's 10s default idle timeout left the pool cold at a 5-min
      probe interval. `allowExitOnIdle` is what makes `idleTimeoutMillis: 0` safe here (nothing
      calls `pool.end()`, so unreaped sockets would hang the Vitest run). `connectionTimeoutMillis`
      added so a Supabase that accepts TCP but never authenticates returns 503 instead of hanging.
- [x] **globalSetup refuses a non-local DB** (`fd9dfed`) — it applies all 10 migrations and seeds
      tenants, and `apps/api/.env` holds the PRODUCTION Supabase URL while Vitest loads `.env` into
      `process.env`. A plain `pnpm --filter @hostyllo/api test` on a dev machine would have seeded
      production. Fails closed, localhost only, no escape hatch. **Do not weaken this.**
- [x] RLS CI gate (§2) · workspace-wide typecheck (`161794a`) · payment extras + audit tests (§0)
      · students.ts JSON-Schema validation (§1.5) — details in each section.

### ⚠️ FINDING — INVARIANT-2/3 ARE NOT ENFORCED (found 2026-07-26, NOT fixed, needs your call)
**`apps/api/eslint.config.js` never loads `eslint-plugin-hostyllo`.** It registers only
`@typescript-eslint`. So `require-with-tenant` and `no-hostel-id-from-request` — the two rules
CLAUDE.md names as the enforcement for INVARIANT-2 and INVARIANT-3 — have **never run in CI**.
`@hostyllo/config` is not even a dependency of `apps/api`, so the config could not import it.

This makes two documented claims false, and they should be corrected either way:
  - CLAUDE.md: "INVARIANT-2 & 3 are the only two checked by the ESLint plugin"
  - PRD Phase 2 entry gate: "`withTenant()` ESLint rule active and blocking violations in CI"

Measured before reporting (probe config, since deleted; `eslint.config.js` untouched):
  - `hostyllo/require-with-tenant` → **90 errors**
  - `hostyllo/no-hostel-id-from-request` → **0 errors** (INVARIANT-3 does look genuinely respected)

NOT wired up, deliberately. The rule matches any `.query/.select/.insert/.update/.delete` member
call, so most of the 90 are legitimate or false positives: privileged-pool use in workers and the
auth bootstrap (correct by design — see migration 010's two connection identities), the test files
and globalSetup, and 2 hits in `lib/crypto.ts`, which has no DB access at all. Turning it on as
`error` today just reddens CI.

**Decision needed:** scope the rule to `src/routes/**` only, or refine it to recognise the
privileged pool, before enabling. That is a design call about where the boundary sits, so it is
yours — see tasks/phase2-proposal.md §3.

