- [x] `PATCH /payments/:id`: recalc with real extras from DB, not hardcoded `[]`
- [x] `audit_log` INSERT on payment create / edit / void-request / void-confirm (INVARIANT-5)
- [x] BONUS: `Number()` coercion on NUMERIC columns in PATCH (pg returns strings → `'10000'+500`
      was string concat = corrupted totals)
- [x] BONUS: migration 003 CHECK said `'voided'` but all code uses `'void'` → void-confirm would
      have violated the constraint at runtime. Migration fixed. ⚠️ If a live DB already has the
      old constraint applied, it needs `ALTER TABLE ... DROP/ADD CONSTRAINT`.
- [x] Integration tests covering extras persistence + audit rows — **DONE 2026-07-26** (`df21115`,
      `apps/api/src/__tests__/payments.test.ts`, 6 tests green in CI). Covers: extra_charges rows
      persisted with label+amount; total_due includes them; payment_created audit row carries the
      extras; PATCH recalculates from the REAL extras (edits to the total that would apply if
      extras were dropped, so the old bug flips both unpaid and status); payment_updated audit row
      holds old+new state; audit_log rejects UPDATE and DELETE (INVARIANT-5, live trigger).

